  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-212963",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x<y-5.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have $6<1-5,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $5≮0-5,$ or equivalently, $5\\ge 0-5,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $2<6-5,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
